# Day 28

## Experiment Title

Monitoring Docker Compose Applications


## Objective

To understand how Docker Compose applications can be monitored using logs and container status information.


## Theory

Monitoring is an important part of containerized application management. Docker Compose provides various methods to monitor running containers, application logs, and service health.

Logs help in identifying errors, tracking application activity, and troubleshooting container issues. Docker Compose also allows users to check container status and observe resource usage through Docker Desktop.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and verify that all required services are running.

Start the Docker Compose application.

Monitor the status of running containers.

View application logs generated by the containers.

Inspect service activity and verify proper execution.

Observe the container details using Docker Desktop.


## Output

Docker Compose application services were monitored successfully.

Container logs displayed application activity correctly.

Running container status and service information were verified successfully.


## Result

Successfully learned how to monitor Docker Compose applications using logs and container status information.
